  "question": {
    "text": "Solubility products $\\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\right)$ of the salts of types $\\mathrm{MX}, \\mathrm{MX}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{M}_{3} \\mathrm{X}$ at temperature $\\mathrm{T}$ are $4.0 \\times 10^{-8}, 3.2 \\times 10^{-14}$ and $2.7 \\times$ $10^{-15}$ respectively. Solubilities (in $\\mathrm{mol} \\mathrm{dm}^{-3}$ ) of the salts at temperature $\\mathrm{T}$ are in the order"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\quad M X>M X_{2}>M_{3} X$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$M_{3} X>M X_{2}>M X$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{MX}_{2}>\\mathrm{M}_{3} \\mathrm{X}>\\mathrm{MX}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{MX}>\\mathrm{M}_{3} \\mathrm{X}>\\mathrm{MX}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{ll}\r\n\\mathrm{MX} & \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=4 \\times 10^{-8}=\\mathrm{S}^{2} \\therefore \\mathrm{S}=2 \\times 10^{-4} \\\\\r\n\\mathrm{MX}_{2} & \\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=3.2 \\times 10^{-14}=4 \\mathrm{~S}^{3}\r\n\\end{array}$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{S}^{3}=\\frac{3.2 \\times 10^{-14}}{4}$\r\n$\\mathrm{~S}^{3}=8 \\times 10^{-15} \\quad \\mathrm{~S}=2 \\times 10^{-5}$\r\n$\\mathrm{M}_{3} \\mathrm{X} \\quad \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}=2.7 \\times 10^{-15}=27 \\mathrm{~S}^{4} \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{S}=10^{-4}$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{MX}>\\mathrm{M}_{3} \\mathrm{X}>\\mathrm{MX}_{2}$"
  }
}